Real battery level on spesn (boot-arg spesbatt=1, default off): SweetBattery polls the sm5602
fuel gauge (I2C 0x71) and the bq2589x-compatible charger (0x6a) on QUP0 SE1 (i2c@4a84000, the
amplifier bus) every 30 s and publishes percent, voltage, current, ExternalConnected, IsCharging
and FullyCharged. Log lines "SPES BATT:".

Read-only towards the chips: the only I2C bytes written are register pointers before a read.
The SoC side (SE1 clock vote, XO RCG, GPIO 4/5 qup1 function, SE1 setup) is the path spes_amp
already uses. Refuses with spesamp set (no lock on SE1) and off /spes-platform. Any failed or
implausible gauge read falls back to the old static 100 %, external power.

Register sources: the stock Android kernel (boot_b) sm5602 driver: register table at Image
offset 0x2647190 (00..0a, 0c..14, 1a, 1b, 62, 73, 74, 90, 91, 95, 96), word reads through
i2c_smbus_read_word_data (low byte first), SOC/voltage/current decode from fg_read_soc,
fg_read_volt and the current reader (sm,rsns = 0 -> x2). bq25890 datasheet register layout;
part numbers 3/1/4 (bq25890/SYV690/SC89890H) as the stock driver's detection.

